==Old English==

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{m|gem-pro|*mēnōþs}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{m|ine-pro|*mēnōt-||month, moon}} < {{m|ine-pro|*mḗh₁n̥s}}. Cognate with Old Frisian {{term|mōnath|lang=ofs}}, Old Saxon {{term|mānuð|lang=osx}}, Dutch {{term|maand|lang=nl}}, Old High German {{term|mānōd|lang=goh}} (German {{term|Monat|lang=de}}), Old Norse {{term|mánaðr|lang=non}} (Danish {{term|måned|lang=da}}, Swedish {{term|månad|lang=sv}}), Gothic {{term|𐌼𐌴𐌽𐍉𐌸𐍃|tr=menoþs|lang=got}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|/ˈmoːnɑθ/|lang=ang}}

====Noun====
